{[%evp 0,100,17,22,21,-4,-8,32767,32767,-88,-50,-70,-72,-53,-94,-162,-79,-44,-80,-57,-19,32767,32767,-67,-74,-118,-77,-32,-89,32767,-104,-71,-90,-119,-85,32767,32767,-148,-144,-143,-174,32767,32767,32767,-164,-162,-160,-177,-152,32767,32767,-190,-198,-172,-153,-171,32767,-160,-154,-180,-186,-193,32767,-177,-144,-106,-165,32767,32767,-145,-140,-123,-159,-127,-176,-153,-141,-135,-146,-141,32767,-148,-140,-143,-148,-138,32767,-155,-138,-118,-119,-173,32767,-89,-85,-105,-111,-121,-87,-85,-95,-213,-180]} {When i checked my opponents earlier games I noticed to my pleasure that he had played a very interesting and risky Kings Gambit, so I played 1, - e5 in order to have some fun!} 1. e4 e5 2. f4 exf4 3. Nf3 g5 4. d4 g4 (4... d6 {see Nightingale-Ruggeri Laderchi}) 5. Bxf4 $5 (5. Ne5 Qh4+ 6. g3 fxg3 7. Qxg4 Qxg4 $1 {is the traditional line of the Rosentreter Gambit, which is probably good for Black.} 8. Nxg4 d5 9. Ne3 dxe4 10. hxg3 (10. Nc3 $1) 10... Nc6 11. Bb5 Bd7 $15 {Bangiev}) 5... gxf3 6. Qxf3 {[#]} Nc6 $1 (6... d5 7. Be5 $1 $18 f6 (7... Bb4+ 8. c3 dxe4 9. Qxe4 Qe7 10. cxb4) (7... Qg5 8. Nc3) 8. Qh5+ Kd7 (8... Ke7 9. Nc3) 9. Bg3) (6... d6 7. Bc4 (7. Nc3 Nc6 8. Bb5 Bd7 $15) 7... Qh4+ 8. Bg3 Qf6 $15) 7. Bc4 (7. d5 Qf6 8. dxc6 Qxb2 9. cxb7 Bxb7 10. Qb3 Bg7 11. c3 Qxa1 12. Qxb7 Bxc3+ 13. Kd1 Rd8 14. Bxc7 Nf6 15. Bxd8 Kxd8 16. Bd3 Ng4 $19) 7... Qh4+ $2 {There goes my advantage!} (7... d5 8. Bxd5 Qh4+ $17) (7... Qf6 $1 8. e5 Qg6 9. c3 d5 (9... d6) 10. exd6 cxd6 11. O-O Nge7 $19) 8. g3 $11 Qe7 9. Nc3 Nxd4 10. Qf2 $2 (10. Qd3 $1 Ne6 11. O-O-O $11) 10... Ne6 {Back in action} 11. O-O-O Nxf4 12. gxf4 Qc5 13. Qe2 b5 14. Bxb5 (14. Nxb5 Rb8 15. c3 Ne7 16. b4 Qb6 17. Qh5 (17. e5 Rg8) 17... Qf6 $19) (14. Bd5 c6 $19) 14... Rb8 15. e5 (15. Rd5 Qb6 16. Rf5 {½-½ Nightingale,D (1790)-Haugen,A (1698)} (16. Re5+ Kd8 17. Na4 Qh6 18. Rf1 Nf6)) 15... Kd8 16. Rhf1 Ne7 17. Rf3 (17. Bxd7 Bxd7 18. e6 Qc6 $19) (17. Kb1 Nf5 $19) 17... c6 18. Bc4 Bh6 19. Bxf7 Rb4 20. e6 {[#] Tough decision here} Bxf4+ $6 (20... Rxf4 $1 21. Kb1 d6 $19 22. Qf1 Qe5 23. Rxf4 Qxf4 24. Qe1 Kc7 25. Nb5+ Kb8 26. Nxd6 Rd8 27. Nxc8 Rxd1+ 28. Qxd1 Nxc8 $19) (20... d6 $1 21. Qd2 Nf5 22. Kb1 Ke7 $19) 21. Kb1 d6 22. a3 Rd4 23. Ne4 Qb5 24. Rfd3 Rxd3 25. Rxd3 Qe5 26. Rxd6+ Kc7 27. Rd3 Nd5 28. Qe1 Kb8 29. Qh1 {[#]} Nb6 $6 (29... Rd8 $1 30. Nc5 Bg5 31. Rb3+ Ka8 32. Qe4 Qxe4 33. Nxe4 Be7 $19) 30. Qf3 Rf8 31. Nc5 Nc4 32. c3 {[#]} Be3 $2 {Missed my second chance!} (32... Kc7 33. Nd7 Qf5 34. Ka1 Ne5 35. Nxe5 Qxe5 36. Rd4 Bg5 37. Re4 Qd6 $19) 33. Nd7+ $1 Bxd7 34. exd7 Nd2+ 35. Rxd2 Bxd2 36. Be8 Rxf3 37. d8=Q+ Kb7 38. Bxc6+ Kxc6 39. Qa8+ Kb6 40. Qxf3 Qe6 41. h4 Be3 42. Kc2 h6 43. a4 Ka5 44. b3 Qe5 45. b4+ Kb6 46. a5+ Kb5 47. Qf1+ Kc6 48. b5+ Kd7 {[#]} 49. b6 axb6 (49... Qe4+ $1 50. Kb2 axb6 51. Qf7+ Qe7 52. Qxe7+ Kxe7 53. axb6 Bxb6 $11) 50. axb6 Bxb6 51. Qf7+ Kc6 {A very interesting game with a few missed chances, but great defense by my Irish friend!} 1/2-1/2

